\(p3\times p_{\rm T}^{-1}+p4\times p_{\rm T}^{-2}\), where \(p0,p1,p2,p3\), and \(p4\) are free parameters. The fit results are shown as red curves in Figs. 4.18 and 4.19. The 68% confidence interval from fitting is used as the statistical uncertainty which is smaller than the line width shown in the figures.

