## Acknowledgements

First and foremost, I would like to convey my deepest appreciation to my advisors, Zebo Tang, Lijuan Ruan, and Rongrong Ma, for their indispensable guidance and consistent support throughout my Ph.D. journey. Zebo, whose mentorship was instrumental in my introduction to the field of heavy ion physics, has been pivotal in shaping my understanding of physics analysis and particle detectors. His teachings have significantly contributed to my academic advancement. Lijuan's meticulous guidance, coupled with her nurturing care for my life and studies at BNL, has truly inspired me. Rongrong has enlightened me with his insightful discussions on physics and analysis techniques, and his expertise and advice have been immensely beneficial. I am also particularly grateful to Zhangbu Xu for the invigorating ideas and insights in physics, which have made my work more engaging. I wish to express special thanks to Rongrong for being a part of my wedding ceremony, a cherished milestone in my life.

